# ALLOWLIST, not a deny list.
#
# A deny list is the wrong shape for a build context: it has to be updated every time
# something new appears in the tree, and the thing that appears is exactly the thing
# nobody thought to exclude. Two concrete cases it was already missing:
#
#   - `.gitignore` excludes `scripts/run_*.sh` and `scripts/_probe*.py` as "throwaway;
#     hardcoded paths", but the Docker build context is the WORKING TREE, not the git
#     tree, and the Dockerfile does `COPY scripts /opt/mumdia/scripts`. A locally built
#     image would have baked them in. (CI builds from a clean checkout, so the published
#     image was never affected -- it was latent, not live.)
#   - untracked local data and vendored comparison sources (`alphadia/`, `lib/`,
#     `raw_files/`, `val*/`, `mbr_work/`) all entered the context and were sent to the
#     daemon on every local build.
#
# Everything is excluded, then the four things the Dockerfile actually COPYs are
# re-included. Adding a new COPY now requires adding it here, which is the failure
# direction we want: a build that misses a file, not an image that carries one.
*

# The workspace the release binary is built from.
!rust
rust/**/target
rust/**/.cargo/config.toml

# The Python sidecar workers the engine invokes, and their environment specs.
!scripts
scripts/__pycache__
scripts/*.pyc
# Local-only helpers with hardcoded paths (mirrors .gitignore).
scripts/run_*.sh
scripts/_probe*.py
!env

# The two baked configs, and the notices that must travel with the binary.
!docker
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md
!sbom.cdx.json
